        "original_id": "b5bc85e5-5a69-58ae-a1de-5a5ccbd2c00f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sidney Olcott, Denis Villeneuve, Gene Gauntier\n- Roles: film producer, director, actor, screenwriter, writer\n- Works: From the Manger to the Cross, Maelström, Polytechnique, Incendies, Enemy\n- Awards: Canadian Screen Award, Genie Award\n\nFacts:\n- Sidney Olcott was born on September 20, 1872, and he was a Canadian-born film producer, director, actor, and screenwriter.\n- Sidney Olcott directed From the Manger to the Cross and also appeared in the film.\n- Gene Gauntier wrote the script for From the Manger to the Cross and portrayed the Virgin Mary in the film.\n- Denis Villeneuve was born on October 3, 1967, and he is a French Canadian film director and writer.\n- Denis Villeneuve won the Canadian Screen Award, formerly called the Genie Award, for Best Direction for Maelström in 2001.\n- Denis Villeneuve won the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction for Polytechnique in 2010.\n- Denis Villeneuve won the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction for Incendies in 2011.\n- Denis Villeneuve won the Canadian Screen Award for Best Direction for Enemy in 2013.\n- Sidney Olcott died on December 16, 1949.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
